      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it's that \"gap\" that's so creepy. and think about the incentive—if they can predict when a user is likely to be impulsive or stressed, they can target ads or even manipulate buying behavior in real-time through their apps. it wouldn't even need to be a massive leak to be happening; they just need a handful of engineers to build the model in secret. if a company has the tech to do it, and there's almost zero oversight on what that biometric data actually represents once it's in their cloud, why should we assume they *aren't* doing it? it's basically the perfect silent surveillance tool.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
